  "id": "decentering",
  "term": "decentering",
  "definition": "Decentering is a metacognitive process in which a person notices thoughts and emotions as temporary mental events rather than as direct facts about the self. It involves stepping back from distressing inner experiences, which can support a more balanced self-view and greater psychological flexibility.",
